According to my etymological dictionary, the Dutch word was borrowed 
from Scandinavian; it is related to the old Norwegian word 'har' 
(shark), and the Gothic word 'hoha' and Old High German word 'huohili', 
the last two meaning 'plough'. It mentions that the animal was probably 
named after the typical back fin, which resembled a plough.

